WEBVTT

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.320
Your monster is wide open!

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.810
Tiger Dragon attacks Speed Warrior!

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.740
Stripe Burst!

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.960
It's almost over.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.790
I set one card and end my turn.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.430
I only have 300 life points left.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:51.780
In order to fight back against Tiger 
Dragon's 2400 attack points...

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.620
My turn!

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.470
I summon Debris Dragon!

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.220
A Tuner Monster?

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.050
When Debris Dragon is successfully summoned,

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:14.750
I can Special Summon a monster in my 
graveyard with 500 or fewer attack points.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.610
I Special Summon Sonic Chick!

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:23.900
Level 4 Debris Dragon tunes Level 3 
Shield Warrior and Level 1 Sonic Chick.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.570
The wishes come together 
to form a new shining star!

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.780
Become the path that lights the way!

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:30.970
Synchro Summon!

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.580
Soar, Stardust Dragon!

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:42.950
You fell into my trap.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:44.680
What?

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:10.580
Meklord Emperor Wisel!

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:17.640
Once a turn, Wisel absorbs a 
Synchro Monster on your field!

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.320
Stardust Dragon!

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:28.240
Just like this speed...

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.760
I'm battling at the edge.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.130
Yusei, don't you also desire 
this type of dueling?

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:41.140
If we battle together, you'll 
be able to find your goal!

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.880
Sherry...

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:50.240
Stop it!

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.360
It was a dream.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:21.100
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:26.630
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:31.110
Don't look back and keep going

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:36.940
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:41.920
There's no need to fear

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:49.590
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:55.600
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:01.370
Streak to the infinite future

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:06.770
Dreams surpass their limits

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:14.880
And will lead you to a bright place

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:47.050
After Sealing Synchro Summoning...

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:49.490
What?

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.370
You want to battle me?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.310
What's going on, Yusei?

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.520
Why do you want to battle Jack?

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.170
I've been thinking about this for awhile.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:04.540
I want to find a new battle method 
that doesn't use Synchro Summons.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.840
A new battle method?

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.950
Do you remember the duel against Ghost?

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.960
The duel against Ghost...

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.700
He sealed away Synchros.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.640
Majestic Dragon saved me back then.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:39.040
But if Ghost appears again, 
I don't know if I can win.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:45.080
That's why I want to find a way to battle 
him without using Synchro Summons.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:46.360
Yusei...

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:52.700
Fine.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.400
I'll face you.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:56.190
But I won't go easy on you.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:05:59.100
All right!  I'll go too!

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.820
Does a new battle method really exist?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.170
Here I go, Yusei!

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.020
Right!

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:15.890
Field Spell Speed World 2 set on!

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.020
Duel Mode on.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.490
Autopilot standby.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.500
Lane selection...

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:29.870
Searching for optimal lane...

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.480
Sending duel lane request to Central.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.840
Authorization!

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.080
Riding Duel!  Acceleration!

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:55.330
My deck has to make optimal use of my Synchro 
Monsters' attack points without summoning them.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:56.560
Therefore...

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:58.260
My turn!

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.090
I summon Shield Wing in defense position!

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:07.500
I set one card and end my turn.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.560
You begin by defending?

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.960
You can't duel like that 
and defeat Jack Atlas!

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.510
My turn!

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:18.530
I summon Twin-Sword Marauder!

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:27.620
When this card attacks a monster in 
defense position, it can attack again!

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:30.930
Twin-Sword Marauder attacks Shield Wing!

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:40.370
Shield Wing can't be destroyed 
in battle up to twice per turn!

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:43.310
But Twin-Sword Marauder deals piercing damage

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:46.710
if its attack points are greater 
than your monster's defense points!

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:54.320
Since it attacked a monster in defense 
position, it attacks Shield Wing again!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.950
Double Assault!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.960
Survive, Shield Wing!

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.800
You take 700 points of piercing damage!

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:10.450
He took damage, but he survived.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:12.400
Not good enough, Yusei!

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:17.340
When my Warrior-Type monster fails 
to destroy your monster in battle,

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:20.040
I can Special Summon this card!

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:22.750
I Special Summon Sword Master!

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:28.550
If two attacks can't destroy it, then 
I just have to attack three times!

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:31.510
Sword Master attacks Shield Wing!

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.620
Master Slash!

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.970
Sword Master also deals piercing damage!

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.970
This is bad.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.140
I end my turn.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.140
Attack me, Yusei!

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.370
My turn!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.380
I summon Junk Synchron from 
my hand in defense position!

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.010
A Tuner Monster!

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.620
When this card is successfully summoned,

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:13.750
I can Special Summon a Level 2-or-below 
monster from my graveyard in defense position!

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.710
I Special Summon Shield Wing!

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:23.130
A Level 3 Tuner and a Level 2 monster.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:27.600
Usually, he would now Synchro 
Summon Junk Warrior.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:31.560
When I have two monsters on 
my field in defense position,

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:34.280
I can Special Summon this card from my hand!

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:37.230
I Special Summon Backup Warrior!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.540
Next, I activate a trap!

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.180
Synchro Deception!

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.070
Since the correct Synchro Material 
Monsters are on the field,

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:49.500
I can send Junk Warrior in my 
Extra Deck to the graveyard.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:54.100
Backup Warrior gains attack points equal 
to half of Junk Warrior's attack points!

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:58.600
Backup Warrior gains 1150 attack points!

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.530
Backup Warrior attacks Sword Master!

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:06.520
Support Attack!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:13.870
I end my turn.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:19.380
So instead of summoning the Synchro Monster,

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:22.780
you're using it to increase 
another monster's attack points.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:26.770
That stops your opponent from 
sealing away your Synchros.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.450
But that's only good enough to 
survive until the End Phase!

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:31.900
My turn!

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.930
I summon Dark Bug from my hand!

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:45.180
When this card is successfully summoned, I can 
Special Summon a Tuner Monster from my graveyard!

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:47.550
I Special Summon Sword Master!

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:54.630
Level 3 Sword Master tunes Level 1 Dark 
Bug and Level 4 Twin-Sword Marauder!

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:58.020
The pulse of the King now forms a line here!

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:00.380
Witness the power of the rumbling heavens!

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.990
Synchro Summon!

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:04.780
My soul!  Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:09.130
Yusei, I'll prove that your ideas are weak!

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:12.940
Red Dragon Archfiend attacks Backup Warrior!

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.650
Absolute Powerforce!

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.160
Jack?

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.590
I'm stopping the duel!

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:33.370
We already know how it's going to end!

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.510
It's a waste of time to continue!

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:39.190
In a duel, power is everything!

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:43.060
No matter who we're facing, we have to 
keep pushing with our Synchro Monsters!

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:45.730
But he can seal away our Synchros.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.750
If he absorbs our Synchro Monsters...

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.720
I'll still win!

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:55.430
Jack...

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:36.800
Wow!

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:41.510
No wonder it's the World Riding 
Duel Grand Prix premiere event!

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.470
Team Unicorn.

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:47.640
They're the Riding Duel team that 
won the Atlantis Tournament.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:50.450
Team Mantis is over there!

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:54.280
Miracles do happen.

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:57.090
I knew Lua wanted to come, 
but I didn't think Aki would.

00:12:57.990 --> 00:12:59.660
Well...

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:04.830
Back then...

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:10.070
Back then, what was Yusei seeing and feeling?

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.280
I want to know more about Riding Duels.

00:13:21.310 --> 00:13:23.440
Is she here tonight?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.520
She said that she would 
also enter the Grand Prix.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:29.120
Yusei!  Everyone!

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.390
Carly, you're here too?

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:32.930
Of course!

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:37.660
It's the World Riding Duel Grand Prix 
premiere event that everyone was waiting for!

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:42.260
Elite teams are here, so 
I'll do a lot of reporting!

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:44.390
By the way, where's Jack?

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:45.590
Jack?

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.380
Come to think of it, he's not here.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:50.720
I thought he would come early and show off.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.540
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.150
What's with those clothes?

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:02.810
I had it specially made for today.

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:04.670
Had it made?

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:07.270
Jack, you're wasting money again!

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:11.330
Do you know how long it 
took to save up that money?

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:15.270
And you don't do any work!  I 
have to make all the deliveries!

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:18.480
It's starting.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:26.890
Thank you for coming to the first-ever World 
Riding Duel Grand Prix premiere event.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:32.140
As you know, Neo Domino City 
has undergone a huge rebirth.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:37.240
With the opening of the Daedalus Bridge, the 
border between City and Satellite has vanished.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:41.990
We've changed into an ideal 
city where anyone can duel.

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:47.750
World Riding Duel Grand 
Prix, or WRGP for short.

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:52.470
This event symbolizes Neo 
Domino City's rebirth.

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:58.140
This huge event is a bridge to 
the future for everlasting peace!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.950
Yusei, I'll prove that your ideas are weak!

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:11.920
Red Dragon Archfiend attacks Backup Warrior!

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.950
Absolute Powerforce!

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:23.040
If I don't use Synchro Summons, I can't 
unleash the true power of my deck.

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:42.590
Allow me to provide details for the 
first-ever World Riding Duel Grand Prix!

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:47.450
The race course is currently under 
construction and circles Neo Domino City's outskirts.

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:49.310
The course can transform!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:54.410
A year from now, D-Wheelers that 
win their regional tournaments

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:59.600
will furiously compete on this 
transforming course in the final round!

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:04.960
The centerpiece will be endurance Riding 
Duels where three people form a team and battle!

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:14.550
The party is a success.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.110
Everyone is very satisfied.

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:18.970
Good job.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:23.150
They don't realize that they're being used.

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:27.330
We're spending a lot of effort.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:31.590
If we want to draw out their power, then 
we should just create chaos ourselves.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:34.700
Everything we do is for more power.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:38.820
These duelists have hidden 
potential that we don't possess.

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:42.750
They'll hone their skills 
to enter the Grand Prix.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:48.360
So when it's time for them to unleash their 
power, they'll emit even greater power.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.090
Yusei Fudo?

00:16:56.370 --> 00:17:00.660
You're Yusei Fudo, the 
winner of the Fortune Cup.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.070
We heard rumors about you.

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:06.810
I'm sorry.  We haven't introduced ourselves.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.850
We're Team Unicorn.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:11.460
Team Unicorn?  I know you!

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:15.270
You're the Riding Duel team that's 
setting the new winning streak record!

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:18.290
You're also entering the WRGP?

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:19.200
Who are you?

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.850
I'm Crow, Yusei's teammate.

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:23.420
Excuse me.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.320
Yusei?

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:26.320
Hey, what's wrong?

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:29.050
He's usually not like that.

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:30.290
Excuse me.

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:34.190
Hey, Yusei!

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.770
Let go of me!

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.160
Why are you so annoyed?

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.700
Is it because of Ghost?

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.350
Bullseye.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:46.910
I understand how you feel, but that was rude.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.230
They came over to introduce themselves.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:51.660
I'm sorry.  Apologize to them for me.

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.600
Who is he?

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:19.130
What an elegant gathering!

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:21.840
That's Dobocle, a hoodlum from the city!

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:25.260
Who cares about the WRGP!

00:18:25.260 --> 00:18:28.760
A Riding Duel isn't for fun!

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:30.210
Capture him!

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:32.460
Outta my way!

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:41.160
This is entertaining.

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:47.420
Aki!

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.470
Get outta my way!

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.460
I summon Black Rose Dragon!

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.650
How dare you...

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:11.130
I'll get you next time!

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.960
Dispatch the Duel Chasers!

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:21.610
A psychic duelist.

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:25.350
I'll have to teach him a lesson.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.990
You can't catch me!

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:47.160
This Duel Disk ID signal is...

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:48.900
It's Ghost!

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:02.240
What?  Ghost?

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:10.740
Stop!  Please!

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:17.130
He finally appeared!

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:21.800
Jack Atlas will crush Ghost!

00:20:35.270 --> 00:20:37.780
You came out of the blue!  That's dangerous!

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.090
What's up with him?

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.260
I remember his eyes.

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:05.010
Let's go, Yusei!

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:09.090
It's pointless to go!

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.350
Even if you leave now, 
the duel is already over.

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:17.350
Even if it's not over, Yusei...

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.960
In your current state, 
you can't defeat Ghost.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:35.440
Unless you overcome your limits.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.170
My limits?

00:21:37.870 --> 00:21:41.180
That's the only way to defeat him.

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:13.900
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:18.910
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:23.810
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:28.820
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:33.690
The cruel god tests us

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:40.630
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:44.500
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:50.370
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:54.300
Bond is the proper word

00:22:54.300 --> 00:23:00.270
As we fight, we understand each other

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:03.240
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:05.470
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:05.470 --> 00:23:10.150
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:10.440 --> 00:23:13.010
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:16.480
You want to party until the morning

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:19.720
At our special place
